# Irie at a glance, for the site's first recording box (site/index.html,
# "opening Irie, typing a task and watching its row"). Three agents are at
# work, one of them shown; a fourth task is typed into the task bar,
# starts, and goes to work; then the cards below are shown in turn, down
# to the new one.
# Film it with docs/demo/record.sh, then cut it with docs/demo/cut.sh;
# the steps are in docs/demo/README.md. 16:10, as the site's boxes are,
# and small enough that the cards still read when the box shows it 672
# pixels wide.
#
# The first Show is followed by two Sleeps, as in close-the-window.reel:
# a window's first terminal can hold its drawing up on a busy Mac.
#
# The phone cut starts on the task bar as the task is typed, then rises
# to the cards as it starts, as the first cut of this reel did.
# cut: site type-1.5 end reached:working+1.5
# cut: phone type-2.4 end
# cut: shot type-2.4 540 0 320 0 0 enter+1.6
# cut: caption type-2.2 type+1.1 top Irie runs your AI coding agents side by side, in one calm view.
# cut: caption type+1.4 end top Type a task. It gets its own worktree and card.
# cut: readme enter-2.5 down+1.5
# cut: sheet type-1.5 type+1.6 enter+1.9 down#2+1 end-0.4
Set Size 1024x640
Set Appearance light
Set Palette evergreen
Set Backdrop E9EBDF
Set TypingSpeed 55ms

Spawn research rate limiting libraries for Go
Spawn @acme-api add rate limiting to the login endpoint
Spawn @acme-web +sonnet fix the flaky checkout test

Sleep 500ms
Show 1
Sleep 1s
Sleep 2.5s
Type "@acme-billing retry failed webhooks"
Sleep 700ms
Enter
Wait working 20s
Sleep 2.5s
Down
Sleep 2.5s
Down
Sleep 2.5s
